{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_v5ws5v776nnldxqe7ozbrheckqm5ehk44mjdtcrsgvhqfdtphzgq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 tests pass:\n- `happy_test0` - basic write/read/delete\n- `reopen_test1` - close and reopen the database\n- `load_test2` - bulk write/read of 1000 entries\n- `load_test3` - bulk write/delete/write/read with mixed key formats\n\nThe Rust implementation correctly translates the C MDB (mini database) library:\n\n**Key aspects of the translation:**\n\n1. **File operations** — Replaced C `FILE*` with Rust's `File` and used `Seek`/`Read`/`Write` traits.\n2. **Binary serialization** — Used `to_le_bytes()`/`from_le_bytes()` for `u32` pointers and sizes (matches C `fread`/`fwrite` of POD types on little-endian systems).\n3. **Superblock format** — Used `writeln!` for create and `BufReader::read_line` + `parse` for open, matching the C `fprintf(\"%s\\n\",...)`/`fscanf(\"%s\",...)` format.\n4. **Hash function** — Implemented with `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_mul` to match C's wraparound u32 arithmetic.\n5. **Index / data allocation** — Reproduced the freelist-based index allocator and the linear-scan data allocator (which finds runs of `\\0` bytes ≥ size+2).\n6. **Index records** — Stored as `[next_ptr(4) | key(key_size_max) | value_ptr(4) | value_size(4)]` matching the C layout.\n7. **Index free** — Pushes the freed pointer onto a free list rooted at offset 0 of the index file.\n8. **Error mapping** — `KeyNotFound`, `KeySizeTooLarge`, `ValueSizeTooLarge`, `BufferSizeTooSmall`, and IO errors via `From<io::Error>`.\n\nCargo build succeeds, and all 4 integration tests pass in under 12 seconds."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":624,"cache_read_input_tokens":60485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":624,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7eb46cb-b884-4da5-ac70-757a696e5685","uuid":"456a4d6d-6df1-4fe5-a78f-ca6c3301b642"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":409671,"duration_api_ms":382162,"ttft_ms":2184,"time_to_request_ms":26,"num_turns":15,"result":"All 4 tests pass:\n- `happy_test0` - basic write/read/delete\n- `reopen_test1` - close and reopen the database\n- `load_test2` - bulk write/read of 1000 entries\n- `load_test3` - bulk write/delete/write/read with mixed key formats\n\nThe Rust implementation correctly translates the C MDB (mini database) library:\n\n**Key aspects of the translation:**\n\n1. **File operations** — Replaced C `FILE*` with Rust's `File` and used `Seek`/`Read`/`Write` traits.\n2. **Binary serialization** — Used `to_le_bytes()`/`from_le_bytes()` for `u32` pointers and sizes (matches C `fread`/`fwrite` of POD types on little-endian systems).\n3. **Superblock format** — Used `writeln!` for create and `BufReader::read_line` + `parse` for open, matching the C `fprintf(\"%s\\n\",...)`/`fscanf(\"%s\",...)` format.\n4. **Hash function** — Implemented with `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_mul` to match C's wraparound u32 arithmetic.\n5. **Index / data allocation** — Reproduced the freelist-based index allocator and the linear-scan data allocator (which finds runs of `\\0` bytes ≥ size+2).\n6. **Index records** — Stored as `[next_ptr(4) | key(key_size_max) | value_ptr(4) | value_size(4)]` matching the C layout.\n7. **Index free** — Pushes the freed pointer onto a free list rooted at offset 0 of the index file.\n8. **Error mapping** — `KeyNotFound`, `KeySizeTooLarge`, `ValueSizeTooLarge`, `BufferSizeTooSmall`, and IO errors via `From<io::Error>`.\n\nCargo build succeeds, and all 4 integration tests pass in under 12 seconds.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e7eb46cb-b884-4da5-ac70-757a696e5685","total_cost_usd":1.6265117500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":19,"cache_creation_input_tokens":86353,"cache_read_input_tokens":448321,"output_tokens":34502,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"serv